const BANK = [
  {"d":"D1","q":"エージェントとワークフローの本質的な違いはどれか。","qEn":"What is the essential difference between an agent and a workflow?","o":["エージェントは経路を実行時に決定し、ワークフローは経路を事前に固定する","エージェントは単一のプロンプトで完結し、ワークフローは複数ステップに分割して処理する","エージェントは経路を事前に固定し、ワークフローは経路を実行時に決定する","エージェントとワークフローはどちらも経路を実行時にモデルが動的に決定する"],"oEn":["An agent decides its path at runtime; a workflow fixes the path in advance","An agent is a single self-contained prompt; a workflow splits the work into multiple steps","An agent fixes its path in advance; a workflow decides the path at runtime","Both agents and workflows have the model decide the path dynamically at runtime"],"a":0,"e":"ワークフローは定義済みコードパス、エージェントはモデルが手順とツールを動的に選ぶ。","eEn":"A workflow is a predefined code path; an agent has the model dynamically choose steps and tools."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"エージェント ループの継続/終了を判断する標準的な手段はどれか。","qEn":"What is the standard way to decide whether an agent loop continues or ends?","o":["usage.output_tokens の値（0 なら継続、正の値があれば終了）","stop_reason（tool_use なら継続、end_turn なら終了）","role フィールド（assistant なら継続、user なら終了）","finish_reason（length なら継続、stop なら終了）"],"oEn":["usage.output_tokens value (0 = continue, positive = end)","stop_reason (tool_use = continue, end_turn = end)","role field (assistant = continue, user = end)","finish_reason (length = continue, stop = end)"],"a":1,"e":"自然言語で終了判定するのはアンチパターン。stop_reason で機械的に判断する。","eEn":"Judging termination via natural language is an anti-pattern; decide mechanically via stop_reason."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"サブエージェントを使う主な利点はどれか。","qEn":"What is the main benefit of using subagents?","o":["コンテキストの分離と専門タスクへの特化","推論速度の向上と応答レイテンシの短縮","親コンテキストの完全な共有と履歴の一元管理","モデル呼び出し回数の削減とトークン課金の一括化"],"oEn":["Context isolation and specialization for focused tasks","Faster inference and reduced response latency","Full sharing of the parent context and unified history management","Fewer model calls and consolidated token billing"],"a":0,"e":"各サブエージェントが独立した窓を持ち、親の文脈を汚染しない。探索的調査に有効。","eEn":"Each subagent has its own window and does not pollute the parent context; useful for exploratory research."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"サブエージェントへ文脈を渡す正しい方法はどれか。","qEn":"What is the correct way to pass context to a subagent?","o":["共有メモリ領域に書き込み参照させる","プロンプトに必要な文脈を明示的に含める","親エージェントのシステムプロンプトを継承させる","会話履歴のIDを渡して自動で復元させる"],"oEn":["Have it read from a shared memory region","Explicitly include the needed context in the prompt","Let it inherit the parent agent's full system prompt and history","Pass a conversation ID and have it auto-restore"],"a":1,"e":"サブエージェントは隔離文脈を持ち親履歴を自動継承しない。明示的な受け渡しが必要。","eEn":"Subagents have isolated context and do not auto-inherit parent history; explicit passing is required."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"サブタスク数が入力ごとに変わる複雑な処理に最適なパターンはどれか。","qEn":"Which pattern best fits complex processing where the number of subtasks varies per input?","o":["評価者・最適化者ループ","オーケストレーター・ワーカー","プロンプトチェイニング","ルーティング（分類振り分け）"],"oEn":["Evaluator-Optimizer loop","Orchestrator-Workers","Prompt chaining","Routing (classification)"],"a":1,"e":"サブタスク数が事前に決まらない場合、オーケストレーターが動的に分割・統合する。","eEn":"When the subtask count isn't fixed in advance, an orchestrator dynamically splits and integrates."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"不可逆・高リスクな操作に対する最も有効な安全設計はどれか。","qEn":"What is the most effective safety design for irreversible, high-risk operations?","o":["リトライ回数を増やして操作の冪等性を確保する","ヒューマン・イン・ザ・ループ（承認ステップ）","サンドボックス内でドライラン実行に限定する","操作前後に自動スナップショットを取得する"],"oEn":["Increase retries to ensure operation idempotency","Human-in-the-loop (an approval step)","Restrict to dry-run execution inside a sandbox","Take automatic snapshots around the operation"],"a":1,"e":"送金やファイル削除など影響の大きい操作の前に人の承認を挟む。","eEn":"Insert human approval before high-impact operations like transfers or file deletion."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"解けないタスクでループが暴走しコストが急増した。最初に追加すべきものはどれか。","qEn":"A loop ran away on an unsolvable task and costs spiked. What should you add first?","o":["停止条件（最大反復回数・トークン上限・タイムアウト）","各ツールへの詳細な説明文と厳密な入力スキーマ検証の追加","出力を逐次要約するサブエージェントの導入","温度を下げて出力の一貫性を高める設定変更"],"oEn":["Stopping conditions (max iterations, token cap, timeout)","More detailed tool descriptions and strict input-schema validation","Introduce a subagent that incrementally summarizes the output","Lower the temperature to make the outputs more consistent"],"a":0,"e":"無限ループ防止には完了・反復上限・タイムアウトのいずれかで確実に停止させる。","eEn":"To prevent infinite loops, stop reliably via completion, an iteration cap, or a timeout."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"評価者・最適化者パターンが適するのはどれか。","qEn":"When is the Evaluator-Optimizer pattern appropriate?","o":["明確な評価基準があり反復で品質が向上するタスク","サブタスクが互いに独立し完全並列で実行できるタスク","入力ごとに必要な手順数が動的に変わるタスク","一度の生成で確定し検証が不要な低リスクタスク"],"oEn":["Tasks with clear evaluation criteria where iteration improves quality","Tasks whose subtasks are mutually independent and can run fully in parallel","Tasks where the number of required steps varies per input","Low-risk tasks settled in one pass that need no verification"],"a":0,"e":"生成と評価を分離し反復改善する。翻訳の精緻化や複雑な検索が典型。","eEn":"Separate generation and evaluation to iterate; typical for refining translations or complex search."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ハブ＆スポーク型のオーケストレーションの特徴はどれか。","qEn":"What characterizes hub-and-spoke orchestration?","o":["各ワーカーが対等に協調し合意形成で意思決定する","調整役が全通信を仲介し分解・委譲・統合を担う","ワーカーが隣接ノードへ結果を順に受け渡す","調整役を持たず各エージェントが自律的に動く"],"oEn":["All workers cooperate as equals and proceed purely by consensus-based decision-making","A coordinator mediates all communication and handles split, delegate, integrate","Each worker passes its results sequentially to the adjacent node in a chain","There is no coordinator; each agent acts autonomously and independently"],"a":1,"e":"中央の調整役がタスクを分解し各ワーカーへ委譲、結果を統合する。","eEn":"A central coordinator splits the task, delegates to workers, and integrates the results."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"PostToolUseフックの典型的な用途はどれか。","qEn":"What is a typical use of a PostToolUse hook?","o":["ツール結果を処理前に正規化・変換する","ツール呼び出し前に引数を検証する","実行結果をログに記録し監査証跡を残す","ツールの実行可否をポリシーで判定する"],"oEn":["Normalize/transform tool results before processing","Validate the arguments before the tool is called","Record execution results to a log and retain an audit trail","Decide whether a tool may run based on policy"],"a":0,"e":"Unix時刻やISO 8601、数値コードの統一などデータ正規化に使う。","eEn":"Used for data normalization such as unifying Unix time, ISO 8601, or numeric codes."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"前提ゲート（強制）の例として正しいものはどれか。","qEn":"Which is a correct example of a prerequisite gate (enforcement)?","o":["在庫確認が成功するまでcreate_orderの実行を保留する","顧客識別が完了するまでprocess_refundを遮断する","認証トークン検証後にのみdelete_recordを許可する","残高照会が終わるまでtransfer_fundsをキューに積む"],"oEn":["Hold execution of create_order until the stock check succeeds","Block process_refund until customer identification completes","Allow delete_record only after auth-token validation","Queue transfer_funds until the balance inquiry finishes"],"a":1,"e":"プログラム的強制により、前段完了まで後段操作を確実にブロックする。","eEn":"Programmatic enforcement reliably blocks later operations until earlier steps complete."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ReActパターンの特徴はどれか。","qEn":"What characterizes the ReAct pattern?","o":["推論と行動を交互に行い思考を言語化しながらツールを使う","全ての行動手順を事前に詳細計画し一括で順に実行していく","推論過程を内部に隠し最終結果だけを出力する","複数の思考経路を並列に展開し多数決で選ぶ"],"oEn":["Alternate reasoning and acting, verbalizing thought while using tools","Plan all action steps in advance in detail and execute them in one batch","Hide the reasoning process internally and output only the final result","Expand multiple reasoning paths in parallel and pick by majority vote"],"a":0,"e":"「考える→行動する→観測する」を繰り返し複雑タスクの精度を上げる。","eEn":"Repeat think → act → observe to improve accuracy on complex tasks."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"エージェントのコスト増大の主因はどれか。","qEn":"What is the main cause of rising agent cost?","o":["ループ反復ごとに蓄積するコンテキストの再送信","システムプロンプトを毎回わずかに書き換える処理","ツール定義のJSONスキーマを毎回添付すること","応答を待つ間のネットワーク遅延の累積"],"oEn":["Re-sending context that accumulates each loop iteration","Slightly rewriting the entire system prompt on every single turn","Attaching the tools' JSON schema on every request","Accumulated network latency while awaiting responses"],"a":0,"e":"各ターンで履歴全体を送るため入力トークンが累積。キャッシュや圧縮で緩和。","eEn":"Sending the whole history each turn accumulates input tokens; mitigate with caching or compaction."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"権限最小化（Least Privilege）原則とは。","qEn":"What is the principle of least privilege?","o":["タスク遂行に必要な最小限の権限のみ付与する","将来必要になり得る権限をまとめて先に付与する","役割ごとに標準化した権限セットを一律に付与する","利用頻度の高い権限を既定で有効にしておく"],"oEn":["Grant only the minimum permissions needed to do the task","Grant upfront any permissions that might be needed later","Grant a standardized permission set uniformly per role","Enable frequently used permissions by default"],"a":0,"e":"過剰権限は事故時の被害を拡大する。読み取りで足りるなら書き込みを与えない。","eEn":"Excess permissions widen the damage when accidents happen; if read suffices, don't grant write."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"【まとめ】D1の設計判断で一貫して問われる軸はどれか。","qEn":"[Summary] What axis is consistently asked about in D1 design decisions?","o":["単一エージェントで担うか複数エージェントで分担するか","プログラム的に固定すべきか、モデルに委ねるべきか","同期的に処理するか非同期的に処理するか","オープンソースか商用モデルを採用するか"],"oEn":["Whether to handle it with one agent or split across several agents","Whether to fix it in code or delegate to the model","Whether to process synchronously or asynchronously","Whether to adopt an open-source or a commercial model"],"a":1,"e":"予測可能性が要る部分はコードで固定、柔軟性が要る部分のみモデルへ委ねる。","eEn":"Fix in code where predictability is needed; delegate to the model only where flexibility is needed."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツール選択の主たる根拠となるのはどれか。","qEn":"What is the main basis for tool selection?","o":["ツールの説明文","登録された順番","引数の型定義","戻り値の例示"],"oEn":["The tool's description","The tool's registration order","The tool's argument types","The tool's return examples"],"a":0,"e":"名前・説明・パラメータ記述はプロンプトと同じ重み。説明の質が使用精度を決める。","eEn":"Name, description, and parameter docs carry the same weight as a prompt; description quality drives accuracy."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）が解決する課題はどれか。","qEn":"What problem does MCP (Model Context Protocol) solve?","o":["モデルごとに異なるプロンプト形式の非互換性","ツール連携の個別実装が乱立するN×M問題","ツール呼び出し時のトークン超過エラー","エージェント間の権限昇格リスクの管理"],"oEn":["The incompatibility of prompt formats that differ from model to model","The N×M problem of proliferating per-integration implementations","Frequent token-overflow errors that occur during tool calls","Managing privilege-escalation risk between agents"],"a":1,"e":"共通プロトコルで一度作ったサーバーを複数クライアントで再利用できる。","eEn":"A common protocol lets a server built once be reused across multiple clients."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）が公開する3つの主要要素はどれか。","qEn":"What are the three main elements MCP (Model Context Protocol) exposes?","o":["ツール・メモリ・エージェント","ツール・リソース・プロンプト","リソース・セッション・ログ","プロンプト・スキーマ・キャッシュ"],"oEn":["Tools, memory, agents","Tools, resources, prompts","Resources, sessions, logs","Prompts, schemas, caches"],"a":1,"e":"ツールは実行操作、リソースは参照データ、プロンプトは定型テンプレート。","eEn":"Tools are executable operations, resources are reference data, prompts are reusable templates."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ローカルの社内DBにClaude Codeから接続する最適なトランスポートはどれか。","qEn":"What is the best transport to connect Claude Code to a local internal DB?","o":["stdio（標準入出力）","HTTP/SSE（サーバー送信）","gRPC（遠隔呼び出し）","WebSocket（双方向）"],"oEn":["stdio (standard I/O)","HTTP/SSE (server-sent)","gRPC (remote call)","WebSocket (bidirectional)"],"a":0,"e":"同一マシン上の連携にはstdioが単純・高速。攻撃面も狭い。","eEn":"For same-machine integration, stdio is simple, fast, and has a narrow attack surface."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツールのエラーをモデルに返す利点はどれか。","qEn":"What is the benefit of returning tool errors to the model?","o":["エラー内容をユーザーに即座に通知できる","モデルが原因を理解し自己修正・再試行できる","失敗したツールを自動的に無効化できる","後続の全処理を安全に中断し状態を保存できる"],"oEn":["The error can be reported to the user immediately","The model understands the cause and can self-correct or retry","The failing tool can be disabled automatically","All downstream processing can be safely halted and state saved"],"a":1,"e":"例外で即停止せず構造化エラーを返すと、引数修正や再試行を促せる。","eEn":"Returning a structured error instead of halting lets the model fix arguments and retry."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）エラーのerrorCategoryに含まれる分類はどれか。","qEn":"Which classifications are part of MCP (Model Context Protocol) errorCategory?","o":["transient / validation / permission","syntax / runtime / semantic","network / timeout / retryable","fatal / recoverable / ignorable / deferred"],"oEn":["transient / validation / permission","syntax / runtime / semantic","network / timeout / retryable","fatal / recoverable / ignorable / deferred"],"a":0,"e":"一時的・検証・権限などに分類し、isRetryableで再試行可否を示す。","eEn":"Classified as transient/validation/permission, with isRetryable indicating retry eligibility."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"tool_choiceの「any」の挙動はどれか。","qEn":"What is the behavior of tool_choice 'any'?","o":["モデルが判断し必要なら呼ぶ","必ずいずれかのツールを呼ぶ","複数ツールを同時に必ず呼ぶ","呼ぶ前に必ず確認を求める"],"oEn":["The model decides and calls if needed","Always calls one of the tools","Always calls multiple tools at once","Asks for confirmation before any call"],"a":1,"e":"autoはテキストも返す、anyは必ずツール、強制は特定ツールを名指し。","eEn":"auto may return text, any always calls a tool, forced names a specific tool."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"プロジェクトレベルのMCP（Model Context Protocol）設定ファイルはどれか。","qEn":"Which is the project-level MCP (Model Context Protocol) config file?","o":["./mcp.config.js","./.mcp.json","./mcp.yaml","./.mcprc.json"],"oEn":["./mcp.config.js","./.mcp.json","./mcp.yaml","./.mcprc.json"],"a":1,"e":".mcp.jsonはバージョン管理でチーム共有。~/.claude.jsonは個人・実験用。","eEn":".mcp.json is version-controlled for team sharing; ~/.claude.json is for personal/experimental use."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"MCP（Model Context Protocol）サーバーの認証情報の正しい扱いはどれか。","qEn":"What is the correct handling of MCP (Model Context Protocol) server credentials?","o":["OS のキーチェーンから起動時に取得する","環境変数展開（${GITHUB_TOKEN}等）を使う","専用のシークレット管理サービスに保管し実行時に委譲する","起動フラグ --token で毎回コマンド渡しする"],"oEn":["Fetch them from the OS keychain at startup","Use env-var expansion (e.g. ${GITHUB_TOKEN})","Store them in a dedicated secrets-management service and delegate at runtime","Pass them each time via a --token launch flag"],"a":1,"e":"秘密を埋め込まず環境変数で扱う。漏えいは重大リスク。","eEn":"Don't embed secrets; handle them via environment variables. Leakage is a serious risk."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"組み込みツールGrepとGlobの違いはどれか。","qEn":"What is the difference between the built-in Grep and Glob tools?","o":["Grepは内容検索、Globはパスパターン一致","Grepはファイル名検索、Globは全文検索","Grepは正規表現置換、Globはディレクトリ作成","Grepはパス一致、Globは内容検索"],"oEn":["Grep searches content; Glob matches path patterns","Grep searches filenames; Glob does full-text search","Grep replaces via regex; Glob creates directories","Grep matches paths; Glob searches content"],"a":0,"e":"Grepは中身を探す、Globは名前で探す。","eEn":"Grep finds by content; Glob finds by name."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"認証と認可の正しい区別はどれか。","qEn":"What is the correct distinction between authentication and authorization?","o":["認証は暗号化、認可は復号処理のこと","認証は本人確認、認可は権限確認","認証はセッション管理、認可はログ記録","認証はトークン発行、認可はトークン失効"],"oEn":["Authn is encryption; authz is decryption","Authn checks identity; authz checks permission","Authn manages user sessions; authz records access logs","Authn issues tokens; authz revokes tokens"],"a":1,"e":"認証=誰か、認可=何ができるか。両者を区別して設計する。","eEn":"Authentication = who you are; authorization = what you can do. Design them separately."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ツールが18個ある場合と4-5個の場合の違いはどれか。","qEn":"What differs between having 18 tools versus 4-5 tools?","o":["多いほど選択信頼性が低下する","多いほど応答速度が向上する","少ないほど誤呼び出しが増える","個数は選択精度に影響しない"],"oEn":["More tools lower selection reliability","More tools improve response speed","Fewer tools cause more misfires","Tool count does not affect selection accuracy"],"a":0,"e":"役割が重複するツールはモデルを迷わせる。明確で少数のツールが精度を高める。","eEn":"Overlapping tools confuse the model; few, clear tools improve accuracy."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"【まとめ】D2が一貫して問う設計原則はどれか。","qEn":"[Summary] What design principle does D2 consistently ask about?","o":["高速化・並列化・キャッシュ活用","最小権限・明確な定義・構造化結果","広い権限・柔軟な定義・自由な出力","多数のツール・詳細なログ・冗長化"],"oEn":["Speedup, parallelization, cache utilization","Least privilege, clear definitions, structured results","Broad permissions, flexible definitions, free-form output","Many tools, highly detailed logging, and redundancy"],"a":1,"e":"権限を絞り、定義を明確にし、結果を構造化する。三者が堅牢な連携の基盤。","eEn":"Limit permissions, clarify definitions, structure results—these three underpin robust integration."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"CLAUDE.mdの役割はどれか。","qEn":"What is the role of CLAUDE.md?","o":["プロジェクト固有の指示・規約を常時与えるメモリ","実行時に動的読み込みするツール定義のカタログファイル","会話ごとに自動生成される一時的なキャッシュ","モデルの応答例を蓄積する学習用データセット"],"oEn":["A memory that always supplies project-specific instructions and conventions","A catalog file listing tool definitions that are loaded dynamically at runtime","A temporary cache that is auto-generated for each new conversation","A training dataset that accumulates the model's response examples"],"a":0,"e":"ビルド手順や規約を記述し、各セッションで自動的に読み込まれる。","eEn":"It records build steps and conventions and is loaded automatically each session."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"CLAUDE.md設定階層の正しい並びはどれか。","qEn":"What is the correct order of the CLAUDE.md config hierarchy?","o":["ユーザー・プロジェクト・ディレクトリ","グローバル・ローカル・一時セッション","システム・チーム・個人プロファイル","組織・リポジトリ・ブランチ設定"],"oEn":["User, project, directory","Global, local, temporary session","System, team, personal profile","Org, repository, branch settings"],"a":0,"e":"ユーザーは個人専用、プロジェクトはチーム共有、ディレクトリは局所規約。","eEn":"User is personal, project is team-shared, directory is local convention."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"フックとスラッシュコマンドの違いはどれか。","qEn":"What is the difference between hooks and slash commands?","o":["フックは自動発火、スラッシュコマンドは手動呼び出し","フックはUI描画用、スラッシュコマンドはAPI呼び出し用","フックは手動登録、スラッシュコマンドは自動検出される","フックは同期実行、スラッシュコマンドは非同期実行"],"oEn":["Hooks auto-fire; slash commands are invoked manually","Hooks render the UI; slash commands call APIs","Hooks are registered manually; slash commands are auto-detected","Hooks run synchronously; slash commands run asynchronously"],"a":0,"e":"フックはイベント駆動で確実に走り、コマンドは利用者が明示的に起動する。","eEn":"Hooks run reliably on events; commands are explicitly invoked by the user."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"大規模なアーキテクチャ変更に適すモードはどれか。","qEn":"Which mode suits large architectural changes?","o":["オート編集","プラン モード","ヘッドレス実行","対話チャット"],"oEn":["Auto-edit","Plan mode","Headless run","Chat mode"],"a":1,"e":"プランモードで変更前に探索・設計し手戻りを防ぐ。","eEn":"Plan mode lets you explore and design before changing, avoiding rework."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"ヘッドレスモードがCI/CDに適する理由はどれか。","qEn":"Why is headless mode suited to CI/CD?","o":["人の介在なしにコマンドとして実行できる","対話プロンプトを逐次表示して確認できる","リッチなUIでログを可視化できる","GPUを占有して並列処理を高速化できる"],"oEn":["It runs as a command without human intervention","It can display interactive prompts step by step for confirmation","It visualizes logs and output in a rich interactive UI","It monopolizes the GPU to speed up parallel processing"],"a":0,"e":"プルリクの自動レビューやコード生成をパイプラインに組み込める。","eEn":"It embeds automated PR review and code generation into the pipeline."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"スキルとCLAUDE.mdの違いはどれか。","qEn":"What is the difference between a Skill and CLAUDE.md?","o":["スキルはオンデマンド呼び出し、CLAUDE.mdは常時読み込み","スキルは自動発火、CLAUDE.mdは手動でのみ有効化される","スキルはグローバル固定、CLAUDE.mdはセッション限定","スキルは常時読み込み、CLAUDE.mdはオンデマンド呼び出し"],"oEn":["A Skill is invoked on demand; CLAUDE.md is always loaded","A Skill auto-fires; CLAUDE.md is enabled only manually","A Skill is globally fixed; CLAUDE.md is session-scoped","A Skill is always loaded; CLAUDE.md is invoked on demand"],"a":0,"e":"スキルはタスク特化ワークフローを必要時に呼ぶ。CLAUDE.mdは普遍的標準。","eEn":"A Skill calls a task-specific workflow when needed; CLAUDE.md is the universal standard."},
  {"d":"D3","q":".claude/rules のパススコープの仕組みはどれか。","qEn":"How does the path scope of .claude/rules work?","o":["YAMLのpathsグロブで条件読み込み","ファイル拡張子の自動判定で読み込み","gitignore と同じ除外規則で読み込み","ディレクトリ深さの閾値で読み込み"],"oEn":["Conditional loading via YAML paths globs","Loading by automatic file-extension detection","Loading by the same exclusion rules as gitignore","Loading by a directory-depth threshold"],"a":0,"e":"型別に全域へ適用できる。場所でなく型で適用。","eEn":"Apply by type across the codebase—by type, not by location."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"SKILL.mdのcontext: forkの意味はどれか。","qEn":"What does context: fork in SKILL.md mean?","o":["隔離されたサブ文脈で実行する","親文脈をそのまま引き継いで実行する","複数プロセスに分岐して並列実行する","実行結果を親に自動マージする"],"oEn":["Run in an isolated sub-context","Run inheriting the parent context as-is","Fork into processes and run in parallel","Auto-merge the results back into the parent"],"a":0,"e":"隔離文脈で実行し、allowed-toolsでツール制限、argument-hintで引数を促す。","eEn":"Runs in isolated context; allowed-tools limits tools and argument-hint prompts for arguments."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"権限の推奨許可方針はどれか。","qEn":"What is the recommended permission-granting policy?","o":["読み取りは狭く、書き込みは広く、破壊的は自動許可","読み取りは広く、書き込みは狭く、破壊的は承認必須","全操作を実行前に一律で承認フローに回す","頻度の高い操作から順に権限を緩めていく"],"oEn":["Read narrowly, write broadly, destructive auto-allowed","Read broadly, write narrowly, destructive requires approval","Route every operation through a uniform pre-approval flow","Loosen permissions starting from the most frequent operations"],"a":1,"e":"リスクの非対称性に応じて配分する。調査は安全だが変更は事故を生む。","eEn":"Allocate by risk asymmetry: investigation is safe, but changes cause incidents."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"カスタム スラッシュ コマンドの定義方法はどれか。","qEn":"How do you define a custom slash command?","o":["コマンド用ディレクトリにMarkdownファイルを置く","設定ファイルにコマンド名と本文をJSONで登録する","専用のPythonスクリプトを実装し関数をコマンドとして公開する","起動時フラグでコマンド定義のパスを指定する"],"oEn":["Place a Markdown file in the commands directory","Register the command name and body as JSON in a config file","Implement a dedicated Python script exposing it as a command","Specify the path to the command definition via a launch flag"],"a":0,"e":"ファイル名がコマンド名、本文がプロンプト。$ARGUMENTS等で引数も使える。","eEn":"The filename is the command name and the body is the prompt; arguments work via $ARGUMENTS, etc."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"非対話モードで構造化出力を得るオプションはどれか。","qEn":"Which option gets structured output in non-interactive mode?","o":["--output-format json / --json-schema","--stream --raw / --no-color","--format=text --pretty-print","--structured --emit yaml / --schema-file"],"oEn":["--output-format json / --json-schema","--stream --raw / --no-color","--format=text --pretty-print","--structured --emit yaml / --schema-file"],"a":0,"e":"-p/--printで非対話実行し、JSON出力やスキーマ強制でスクリプト連携する。","eEn":"Run non-interactively with -p/--print and integrate via JSON output or schema enforcement."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"テスト駆動開発（TDD）をClaude Codeで行う流れはどれか。","qEn":"What is the flow for doing TDD with Claude Code?","o":["先にテストを書かせ、それを満たすコードを生成させる","先に詳細な設計書を書かせ、それを実装コードへ自動変換させる","コードを生成後に網羅的なテストを追加させる","実装とテストを一度のプロンプトで同時生成させる"],"oEn":["Write tests first, then generate code that satisfies them","Write a design doc first, then auto-convert it into implementation code","Generate the code first, then add exhaustive tests afterward","Generate the implementation and tests together in a single prompt"],"a":0,"e":"失敗するテストを基準に進める。テストが客観的な完了条件になる。","eEn":"Proceed against failing tests; the tests become an objective completion criterion."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"settings.jsonの役割はどれか。","qEn":"What is the role of settings.json?","o":["権限・フック・環境設定をファイルで管理する","会話履歴とツール出力を保存する記録専用ファイル","モデルの重みとハイパーパラメータを定義する","実行時のトークン使用量を計測する設定"],"oEn":["Manage permissions, hooks, and environment settings via a file","A file dedicated to storing conversation history and tool outputs","Define the model's weights and hyperparameters at load time","A setting that measures runtime token consumption"],"a":0,"e":"プロジェクト単位とユーザー単位で持て、共有設定と個人設定を分離できる。","eEn":"It can be held per project and per user, separating shared and personal settings."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"【まとめ】D3が一貫して問う判断軸はどれか。","qEn":"[Summary] What decision axis does D3 consistently ask about?","o":["確実性が要る処理はフックや権限で固定、柔軟性が要る処理はモデルに委ねる","確実性が必要な処理も柔軟な処理も全てフックと権限で固定して完全に自動化する","処理の種類を問わず全ての判断をモデルに一任し設定を最小化する","コストが最も安いモデルを常に選ぶことだけを基準にする"],"oEn":["Fix certainty-needing work with hooks/permissions; delegate flexible work to the model","Fix both certainty-needing and flexible work entirely with hooks and permissions to fully automate","Delegate every decision to the model regardless of type and minimize configuration","Always pick the cheapest available model as the sole deciding criterion"],"a":0,"e":"CLAUDE.mdで文脈を、権限とフックでガードレールを与える配分が核心。","eEn":"The core is allocating context via CLAUDE.md and guardrails via permissions and hooks."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"プロンプトで「明確さ」が最重要とされる理由はどれか。","qEn":"Why is clarity considered most important in prompting?","o":["曖昧な指示はモデルの解釈を分散させ精度を下げるから","詳細な指示はトークン消費を抑え応答速度を高めるから","明確な指示はモデルの学習データを更新できるから","曖昧な指示はコンテキスト窓を余分に消費するから"],"oEn":["Vague instructions scatter the model's interpretation and lower accuracy","Detailed instructions reduce token consumption and improve response speed","Clear instructions let the model update its training data","Vague instructions consume extra context window capacity"],"a":0,"e":"何を・どの形式で・どこまで求めるかを具体化し誤解の余地を消す。","eEn":"Specify what, in what format, and how far, to eliminate room for misinterpretation."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"一貫した出力を得る最有効な手段の一つはどれか。","qEn":"What is one of the most effective ways to get consistent output?","o":["少数例示（フューショット）","システムプロンプトの詳細化","出力トークン数の上限拡大","長いコンテキストの投入"],"oEn":["Few-shot examples","Detailed system prompt","Raise output token cap","Long context input"],"a":0,"e":"2-4例で選択理由を示し、曖昧ケースの判断を汎化させる。","eEn":"Show 2-4 examples with reasons to generalize judgment on ambiguous cases."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"構文エラーを排し確実な構造化出力を得る方法はどれか。","qEn":"How do you eliminate syntax errors and get reliable structured output?","o":["正規表現による出力の後処理抽出","tool_use＋JSONスキーマ","プロンプト内でJSON形式の出力を依頼","temperatureを0に固定"],"oEn":["Post-process output with regex","tool_use + JSON schema","Ask for JSON in the prompt","Fix temperature to zero"],"a":1,"e":"スキーマで形式を強制すれば構文エラーが排除され確実。","eEn":"Forcing the format via schema eliminates syntax errors and ensures reliability."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"値の捏造（幻覚）を防ぐスキーマ設計はどれか。","qEn":"Which schema design prevents fabricating values (hallucination)?","o":["既定値を全てのフィールドに設定する","nullableフィールドを使う","説明文をフィールドに付与する","列挙型で選択候補を限定する"],"oEn":["Set defaults on every field","Use nullable fields","Add descriptions to fields","Limit choices with an enum"],"a":1,"e":"値が無い場合にnullを許せば、無理に値を埋める捏造を防げる。","eEn":"Allowing null when no value exists prevents forced fabrication of values."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"拡張可能な分類を実現するenumの工夫はどれか。","qEn":"What enum technique enables extensible classification?","o":["自由記述のフィールドだけで分類を表現する","enum＋\"other\"＋detail","enumに全候補を事前列挙する","数値コードのみで分類を表現する"],"oEn":["Use only a free-text field","enum + \"other\" + detail","Pre-list all cases in the enum","Use numeric codes for classes"],"a":1,"e":"許可値に制限しつつotherで未知パターンに対応する。","eEn":"Restrict to allowed values while handling unknown patterns via 'other'."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"スキーマ検証で防げないものはどれか。","qEn":"What can schema validation NOT prevent?","o":["必須フィールドの欠落や列挙値の範囲外といった構造上の形式的な誤り","意味エラー（calculatedとstatedの不一致等）","文字列型のフィールドに数値が混入するような型違反","JSON構文の破綻や閉じ括弧の欠落による解析不能"],"oEn":["Missing required fields or out-of-range enum values","Semantic errors (e.g. calculated vs stated mismatch)","Type violations like a number in a string field","Broken JSON syntax or a missing closing brace that blocks parsing"],"a":1,"e":"スキーマは構文・型・必須は防げるが、意味的な矛盾は別途検証が必要。","eEn":"Schemas catch syntax/type/required issues, but semantic contradictions need separate verification."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"Message Batches APIの特徴はどれか。","qEn":"What characterizes the Message Batches API?","o":["50%節約・最大24時間・SLA保証なし","即時応答で追加料金が発生する同期処理API","常にリアルタイムのストリーミング配信","料金が2倍で優先処理される高速枠"],"oEn":["50% savings, up to 24h, no SLA guarantee","A synchronous API with instant response, premium pricing","Always real-time streaming delivery","A fast tier at double price with priority processing"],"a":0,"e":"夜間レポートや週次監査など待てる処理向け。リクエスト内マルチターンは不可。","eEn":"For deferrable work like nightly reports or weekly audits; no multi-turn within a request."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"肯定形の指示が推奨される理由はどれか。","qEn":"Why are positive (affirmative) instructions recommended?","o":["「するな」より「せよ」のほうが従いやすい","肯定形のほうが出力トークンを節約できるから","否定形はモデルの推論速度を大きく下げるから","肯定形は禁止事項を書かずに済むから"],"oEn":["'Do' is easier to follow than 'don't'","Affirmative form saves output tokens","Negative form greatly slows the model's reasoning","Affirmative form avoids writing prohibitions"],"a":0,"e":"否定形は解釈が不安定。望ましい行動を直接示す。","eEn":"Negative forms are unstable to interpret; state the desired behavior directly."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"システム プロンプトの役割はどれか。","qEn":"What is the role of the system prompt?","o":["モデルの役割・制約・基本方針を会話全体に設定する","直近のユーザー発言だけに一時的な追加指示を与える","会話履歴を要約してトークンを節約する機能","ツールの一覧と各引数のスキーマを定義する"],"oEn":["Set the model's role, constraints, and policy for the whole conversation","Give a temporary additional instruction only to the most recent user message","Summarize the conversation history to conserve context tokens","Define the tool list and the schema of each tool argument"],"a":0,"e":"口調・専門性・禁止事項を定義。個別メッセージより上位の文脈として作用する。","eEn":"It defines tone, expertise, and prohibitions, acting as context above individual messages."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"XMLタグをプロンプトで使う利点はどれか。","qEn":"What is the benefit of using XML tags in prompts?","o":["指示・文脈・例の境界を明確に区切れる","モデルの出力を必ずXML形式に固定できる","入力トークン数を自動的に圧縮できる","推論の途中経過をログに保存できる"],"oEn":["Clearly delimit instructions, context, and examples","Force the model's output into XML format","Automatically compress the input token count","Save the intermediate reasoning steps to an external log"],"a":0,"e":"モデルが各部分を正確に識別できる。Claudeは構造化タグの解釈に強い。","eEn":"The model identifies each part accurately; Claude is strong at interpreting structured tags."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"プレフィルの効果はどれか。","qEn":"What is the effect of prefilling?","o":["応答冒頭を固定し形式逸脱や前置きを抑える","応答末尾に定型の署名文を自動的に付与する","モデルの温度を内部的に自動調整する","会話履歴を圧縮して文脈量を削減する"],"oEn":["Fix the response opening to curb format deviation and preamble","Automatically append a fixed template signature to the response's end","Internally auto-tune the model's sampling temperature","Compress conversation history to reduce context size"],"a":0,"e":"{を入れてJSON出力を強制するなど、出だしを決めて誘導する。","eEn":"Guide by setting the start, e.g. inserting { to force JSON output."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"思考の連鎖（CoT）を常用すべきでない場面はどれか。","qEn":"When should you NOT routinely use Chain of Thought (CoT)?","o":["単純で即答できるタスク","多段の論理推論を要する課題","制約が多い計画立案タスク","複雑な数式の段階的計算"],"oEn":["Simple tasks answerable instantly","Problems needing multi-step logical reasoning","Planning tasks with many constraints","Step-by-step computation of complex formulas"],"a":0,"e":"推論を強制するとトークンとレイテンシが無駄に増える。複雑タスクに限定する。","eEn":"Forcing reasoning wastes tokens and latency; limit it to complex tasks."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"独立レビューインスタンスが自己レビューより優れる点はどれか。","qEn":"How is an independent review instance better than self-review?","o":["生成時の推論文脈を持たず微妙な問題を客観検出できる","同一モデルを使うため出力が完全に一致する","生成時の推論文脈を共有して速く判断できる","レビュー専用の追加プロンプトを設計する手間が一切不要になる"],"oEn":["Without generation context, it objectively detects subtle issues","Using the same model makes the outputs match exactly","Sharing the generation reasoning context lets it judge much faster","It removes all need to design a separate review prompt"],"a":0,"e":"生成者は自分の判断を疑いにくい。独立インスタンスは客観的。","eEn":"The generator rarely doubts its own judgment; an independent instance is objective."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"【まとめ】D4が一貫して強調する原則はどれか。","qEn":"[Summary] What principle does D4 consistently emphasize?","o":["明確・簡潔・例示・形式指定で曖昧さを排す","常に詳細な背景説明を可能な限り多く盛り込む","推論はモデルの自由な解釈に委ねる","出力形式を指定せず自然文で受け取る"],"oEn":["Eliminate ambiguity via clarity, brevity, examples, and format specs","Always pack in the maximum amount of detailed background context possible","Leave the reasoning to the model's free interpretation","Specify no output format and accept plain natural prose"],"a":0,"e":"役割・文脈・タスク・形式を揃え、評価セットで測定しながら反復改善する。","eEn":"Align role, context, task, and format, and iterate while measuring with an eval set."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"コンテキスト窓とは何か。","qEn":"What is the context window?","o":["モデルが一度に処理できる入出力トークンの総量","モデルの事前学習に用いた訓練データ全体の総量","1秒あたりに生成できるトークンの数","同時に呼び出せるツールの最大登録数"],"oEn":["The total input/output tokens the model can process at once","The total amount of training data used to pretrain the model","The number of tokens it can generate per second","The maximum number of tools you can register at once"],"a":0,"e":"窓を超える情報は扱えない。長い対話や大規模文書では管理が必須。","eEn":"Information beyond the window can't be handled; management is essential for long dialogues or large documents."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"「lost in the middle」現象とは何か。","qEn":"What is the 'lost in the middle' phenomenon?","o":["長文の中間部の情報が参照されにくくなる","入力の先頭付近に置いた情報ほど無視される","長文になると出力が途中で打ち切られる","末尾の情報ほど誤って要約される"],"oEn":["Mid-text information becomes less likely to be referenced","Information placed near the very start is most often ignored","With long text, output gets cut off partway","Information near the end is most often mis-summarized"],"a":0,"e":"重要情報は冒頭や末尾に置く。中間に埋めると見落とされやすい。","eEn":"Put key info at the start or end; buried in the middle it's easily missed."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"頻繁に更新される製品情報に基づき回答させる最適手法はどれか。","qEn":"What is the best method to answer based on frequently updated product info?","o":["モデルの再ファインチューニング","RAG（検索拡張生成）","システムプロンプトへの直書き","少数例の追加提示"],"oEn":["Periodic re-fine-tuning of the model","RAG (retrieval-augmented generation)","Hard-coding facts into the system prompt","Adding a few in-context examples"],"a":1,"e":"実行時に最新情報を取得して文脈に加える。再訓練不要で更新に即応、出典提示も可能。","eEn":"Fetch the latest info at runtime and add it to context; no retraining, instant updates, and citable."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"数日にわたるタスクでセッションをまたいで状態を保持する手段はどれか。","qEn":"How do you retain state across sessions for a multi-day task?","o":["メモリツール（外部ストアへの永続化）","システムプロンプトへの全履歴の埋め込み","コンテキスト窓の拡張だけで保持する","毎回プロンプトを冒頭から再送する"],"oEn":["Memory tool (persistence to an external store)","Embedding the full history into the system prompt","Retaining it via context-window expansion alone","Resending the prompt from the top each time"],"a":0,"e":"コンテキスト窓を超えて情報を保存し再参照する。長期タスクの一貫性を支える。","eEn":"Store info beyond the context window and re-reference it; supports consistency on long tasks."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"一時的なAPI失敗への最適な信頼性対策はどれか。","qEn":"What is the best reliability measure for transient API failures?","o":["指数バックオフ付きリトライ（上限あり）","固定間隔での上限なしの再試行","失敗時に即座に処理全体を中断する","temperatureを上げて再送する"],"oEn":["Retry with exponential backoff (capped)","Unlimited retries at a fixed interval","Immediately abort the whole process on failure","Raise temperature and resend the request"],"a":0,"e":"待機を挟んだ再試行が有効。上限を設け恒久的障害での無限再試行を防ぐ。","eEn":"Retrying with waits is effective; cap attempts to avoid infinite retries on permanent failures."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"依存先の連続障害時に全体遅延を防ぐパターンはどれか。","qEn":"Which pattern prevents overall delay during a dependency's consecutive failures?","o":["無制限のリトライ","サーキット ブレーカー","タイムアウトの延長","同期的な逐次呼び出しの徹底"],"oEn":["Unlimited retries","Circuit breaker","Extending the timeout","Serial blocking calls"],"a":1,"e":"連続失敗時に呼び出しを一時遮断し、障害連鎖と負荷集中を防ぐ。","eEn":"On consecutive failures it temporarily cuts off calls, preventing cascades and load concentration."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"アクセス失敗と有効な空結果の正しい区別はどれか。","qEn":"What is the correct distinction between an access failure and a valid empty result?","o":["空結果は必ず再試行し、アクセス失敗はそのまま受容する","アクセス失敗は再試行判断が必要、空結果はそのまま受容","どちらもエラーとして扱い全処理を中断する","両者を区別せず同じ再試行ロジックにかける"],"oEn":["Always retry empty results and accept access failures as-is","Access failure needs retry judgment; an empty result is accepted as-is","Treat both as errors and immediately abort the process","Apply the exact same retry logic to both cases without distinguishing them"],"a":1,"e":"空を成功と偽装するのはアンチパターン。取れなかったのか、無かったのかを区別する。","eEn":"Disguising an empty as success is an anti-pattern; distinguish 'couldn't fetch' from 'nothing there'."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"エスカレーションの適切な契機はどれか。","qEn":"What is an appropriate trigger for escalation?","o":["モデルの確信度が閾値を下回った時","人の要求・ポリシー欠如・進展不能","応答トークン数が上限に達した時","処理時間が想定より長引いた時"],"oEn":["When the model's confidence drops below a threshold","Human request, missing policy, or no progress","When response tokens hit the limit","When processing takes longer than expected"],"a":1,"e":"感情ベースや自己申告確信度は代理指標として不適。校正が不正確。","eEn":"Emotion-based or self-reported confidence are poor proxies; their calibration is inaccurate."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"プロンプトキャッシュが最も効果的な条件はどれか。","qEn":"When is prompt caching most effective?","o":["毎回大きく異なる長い可変部を大量に送信する場合","固定の接頭辞が大きく同一内容を繰り返し送る","出力トークンが極端に短くなる場合","呼び出すツールの数が非常に多い場合"],"oEn":["Sending a large, entirely different variable part every single time","A large fixed prefix with the same content sent repeatedly","When the output tokens become extremely short","When the number of tools called is very large"],"a":1,"e":"固定部分を先頭に、可変部分を後方に置くとヒット率が最大化する。","eEn":"Putting the fixed part first and the variable part later maximizes the hit rate."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"集計精度の罠（97%が隠すもの）とは何か。","qEn":"What is the aggregate-accuracy trap (what 97% hides)?","o":["全体精度が特定の型別の不調を覆い隠す","全体精度が実際の値より低く算出されてしまう","特定の型だけを過剰に最適化する","サンプル数が少なく分散が大きくなる"],"oEn":["Overall accuracy masks poor performance on a specific type","Overall accuracy gets computed lower than it truly is in reality","It over-optimizes for just one specific type","A small sample size makes the variance large"],"a":0,"e":"全体97%でも特定フィールド型では低精度のことがある。層化無作為抽出で測る。","eEn":"97% overall can hide low accuracy on a specific field type; measure with stratified sampling."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"複数情報源を統合する際の矛盾統計の扱いはどれか。","qEn":"How should you handle conflicting statistics when integrating multiple sources?","o":["新しい方の値だけ採用","出典付きで両論併記する","常に最大値を提示する","多数派の数値に統一する"],"oEn":["Adopt only the newer value","Present both sides with citations","Always present the single maximum value","Unify to the majority figure"],"a":1,"e":"claim-sourceマッピングを統合まで保持し、出典付きで矛盾を提示する。","eEn":"Keep the claim-source mapping through integration and present the conflict with citations."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"探索中に文脈を削減する手段はどれか。","qEn":"What reduces context during exploration?","o":["/compact","/reset-all","/verbose","/expand"],"oEn":["/compact","/reset-all","/verbose","/expand"],"a":0,"e":"探索中の文脈を圧縮。scratchpadファイルで境界を越えて保持も可能。","eEn":"Compacts context during exploration; a scratchpad file can also retain it across boundaries."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"グレースフル デグラデーションとは何か。","qEn":"What is graceful degradation?","o":["一部障害時も機能を縮退させつつ動作を続ける","障害を検知した時点で全機能を即座に完全停止する","全機能を通常どおり完全な状態で維持する","システム全体を自動で再起動して復旧する"],"oEn":["Keep operating with reduced function during partial failure","Immediately shut down all functions the moment a fault is detected","Maintain every function fully in a normal state","Automatically restart the whole system to recover"],"a":0,"e":"全停止を避け部分的に動かす。可用性を保つ設計思想。","eEn":"Avoid a full stop and keep partially running; a design philosophy for availability."},
  {"d":"D5","q":"【まとめ】D5が一貫して問う設計判断はどれか。","qEn":"[Summary] What design decision does D5 consistently ask about?","o":["文脈を常に最大化して全履歴を保持し続けることで精度だけを最優先する","文脈を最小十分に保ち効率化し、検証・再試行・観測で信頼性を担保する","検証や再試行を全て省き応答速度だけを最大限に高める","観測やログを完全に排し内部状態を一切記録せずに動かす"],"oEn":["Always maximize the context and retain the entire history in order to prioritize accuracy above everything else","Keep context minimally sufficient and ensure reliability via verification, retries, and observability","Skip all verification and retries entirely to maximize raw response speed alone","Remove observability and logging and run without recording internal state at all"],"a":1,"e":"過剰な文脈は希薄化とコストを招く。非決定性は検証層・冪等性・フォールバックで囲む。","eEn":"Excess context causes dilution and cost; wrap non-determinism with verification, idempotency, and fallback."}
];

